<!--
  SYNTHETIC Problems section (11450-4) in the ICD-10-primary sender shape.

  Everything here is synthetic. No patient data: the identifiers are made
  up and the codes are published terminology, chosen to match the concepts
  named in the review so the fixture stays traceable to the report.

  The four entries, in order:

    1. ICD-10 primary O09.32  + SNOMED 426403007  in translation  -> MATCHES
    2. ICD-10 primary O98.812 + SNOMED 1621000119101 in translation -> MATCHES
    3. ICD-10 primary Z34.90  + SNOMED 72892002   in translation  -> no match,
       whole entry pruned (proves the fix widens which RULES run, not what
       counts as a match)
    4. conformant SNOMED-primary 76272004, plus a second, unconfigured
       problem under the same concern act -> act survives, and only the
       matching entryRelationship is kept (container-level pruning still
       discriminates inside a matched entry)

  <originalText><reference value="#..."/></originalText> is present on every
  value, as it is in the source documents: the labels live in the narrative,
  not on @displayName. That exercises the by-reference -> by-value inlining
  the reconstruction path performs before it swaps the narrative out.
-->
